Comparison Selectors:
Comparison operators compare a field's value against a specified value.

A. $gt – Greater Than and $lte – Less Than or Equal To
Goal: Find employees whose salary is greater than 90,000 but less than or equal to 120,000.
db.employees.find({
  salary: {
    $gt: 90000,
    $lte: 120000
  }
})

B. $in – In an Array
Goal: Find employees who work in either the HR or Sales department.
db.employees.find({
  department: {
    $in: ["HR", "Sales"]
  }
})

C. $ne – Not Equal
Goal: Find all employees whose status is not "On Leave".
db.employees.find({
  status: {
    $ne: "On Leave"
  }
})

5. Logical Selectors
Logical operators are used to combine multiple query conditions.

A. AND (Implicit)
Goal: Find employees in the Engineering department with a performance score of 4.5 or higher.
db.employees.find({
  department: "Engineering",
  performance_score: {
    $gte: 4.5
  }
})

B. $or – OR Operator
Goal: Find employees who are either in the HR department OR have a salary greater than 100,000.
db.employees.find({
  $or: [
    { department: "HR" },
    { salary: { $gt: 100000 } }
  ]
})

6. Combining Selectors for a Complex Query
Goal: Find all Active employees in either Engineering or Sales departments who were hired before 2024.
db.employees.find({
  status: "Active",
  department: {
    $in: ["Engineering", "Sales"]
  },
  hire_date: {
    $lt: new Date("2024-01-01")
  }
})
